      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC12156342::web::041::3_3_corrosion_properties",
        "PMC12525669::web::006::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "Mechanical wear ruptures or removes the surface oxide film.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC12156342::web::000::abstract"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "Elevated temperature accelerates rupture of the protective oxide layer during wear.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Wear-induced oxide rupture exposes clean, electrochemically dissimilar phases at phase boundaries.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC12156342::web::000::abstract",
        "PMC12156342::web::041::3_3_corrosion_properties"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "Potential differences between dissimilar phases establish localized galvanic cells.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC12156342::web::000::abstract",
        "PMC12156342::web::041::3_3_corrosion_properties"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "Localized galvanic interactions accelerate selective dissolution and localized corrosion.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC12156342::web::041::3_3_corrosion_properties"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "Galvanically accelerated corrosion undermines the alloy's mechanical integrity.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Corrosion-induced weakening intensifies subsequent wear, producing positive feedback between wear and corrosion.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The oxide-rupture and micro-galvanic feedback produces accelerated total degradation under simultaneous high-temperature wear and corrosion.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Loss of the protective oxide layer increases wear through adhesive and abrasive wear mechanisms.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC12156342::web::000::abstract"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "Pronounced micro-galvanic action increases the corrosion response.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC12156342::web::000::abstract",
        "PMC12156342::web::041::3_3_corrosion_properties"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "Relative to the untreated baseline, the alloy without a stabilized film will have increased overall degradation.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "A stabilized oxide film will reduce wear relative to the untreated baseline.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
